{"book":9,"chapter":31,"context":{"chapter":31,"title":"Saul Dies on Gilboa","summary":"The Philistines defeat Israel on Mount Gilboa. Jonathan and two other sons of Saul are killed, and the badly wounded Saul falls on his own sword. The Philistines hang the bodies on the wall of Beth-shan, but the men of Jabesh-gilead rescue them by night and bury them.","background":"Mount Gilboa overlooks the eastern Jezreel Valley, and Beth-shan stood where that valley meets the Jordan. The men of Jabesh-gilead repaid Saul's rescue of their town at the start of his reign (ch. 11). The first chapter of 2 Samuel gives an Amalekite's differing claim about Saul's death.","customs":[{"term":"These uncircumcised","verses":"31:4","note":"A term of contempt for the Philistines, who did not practice circumcision. Saul feared being captured and abused by them."},{"term":"Fasted seven days","verses":"31:13","note":"A full week of mourning, the honor given to a respected leader."}],"watchFor":["Saul fears humiliation more than death (v. 4).","The book that opened with a birth ends with deaths.","The loyalty of Jabesh-gilead (vv. 11–13)."],"connections":["1 Samuel 11:1-11","1 Samuel 28:19","2 Samuel 1:6-10","1 Chronicles 10:1-14"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וּפְלִשְׁתִּים","ufelishtim","H6430","HC/Ngmpa","and [the] Philistines"],["נִלְחָמִים","nilchamim","H3898","HVNrmpa","[were] fighting"],["בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל","beyisra'el","H3478","HR/Npl","against Israel"],["וַיָּנֻסוּ","vaiyanusu","H5127","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they fled"],["אַנְשֵׁי","'anshei","H582","HNcmpc","[the] men of"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"],["מִפְּנֵי","mipenei","H6440","HR/Ncmpc","from before"],["פְלִשְׁתִּים","felishtim","H6430","HNgmpa","[the] Philistines"],["וַיִּפְּלוּ","vaiyipelu","H5307","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they fell"],["חֲלָלִים","chalalim","H2491","HAampa","slain"],["בְּהַר","behar","H2022","HR/Ncmsc","on [the] mountain of"],["הַגִּלְבֹּעַ","hagilboa'","H1533","HTd/Npl","<the> Gilboa"]],"x":[[13010001,13010012,7